  message: "Fixed in PR #2200. Re-ran the filed repro: `private const`, `protected const` read visibility=public and exported on dev; now SECRET is private and GUARDED protected, not exported, and public / unmodified / `final public` / interface constants stay public (an enum's `private const` is private). Rule: only private and protected enter the id's visibility slot; an explicit `public const` hashes like an unmodified one. koel: 14 class constants moved (the 14 `private const`), dead-code output byte-identical. NOT DONE (filed): enum cases are not symbols; a typed constant's type is not hashed; methods and properties hash an explicit `public` differently from none. The change moves stable ids, so it shipped in the stableid v14 -> v15 bump; the spec's history row lists the rule and the measured share. Repro record (both arms, commands and copied outputs): ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr2/tracker/repros.md; per-package detail: pr2/STATUS.md; churn: pr2/final_measure.txt."  # 22f5
